WEBVTT

00:00:00.204 --> 00:00:03.806
Second Nature gives small creative
teams a

00:00:03.806 --> 00:00:06.789
repeatable way to turn one visual idea

00:00:06.789 --> 00:00:08.241
into a finished film.

00:00:08.465 --> 00:00:10.911
Start with the featured animation.

00:00:11.099 --> 00:00:13.599
A single drop races through a
precision

00:00:13.599 --> 00:00:17.040
machine, pauses above a waiting seed,
and

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.305
brings it to life.

00:00:18.456 --> 00:00:21.010
Continue as a guest, or create an

00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:24.531
account to keep your workspace across
devices.

00:00:24.719 --> 00:00:27.555
Name a production, choose the drop and

00:00:27.555 --> 00:00:30.606
enamel colors, and set a detail seed

00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:32.031
for consistent soil.

00:00:32.275 --> 00:00:35.850
Save the production, then select
Create film.

00:00:36.092 --> 00:00:39.157
Blender builds and lights the editable
scene,

00:00:39.304 --> 00:00:41.898
renders the complete story in the
cloud,

00:00:42.019 --> 00:00:43.486
and assembles the movie.

00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:46.738
The workbench shows actual frame
progress and

00:00:46.738 --> 00:00:49.883
production logs. Cancel safely if

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:53.633
needed, then resume from completed
frames instead

00:00:53.633 --> 00:00:54.722
of starting again.

00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:57.030
Once finished, play the film in your

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.108
browser and download the video or
Blender

00:01:00.108 --> 00:01:02.917
scene. Download the files you want to

00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:06.465
keep; cloud exports remain available
for seven

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:10.038
days. Created by Shivam Gupta with AI

00:01:10.038 --> 00:01:13.290
assistance, Second Nature connects a

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.785
carefully directed visual story to a
repeatable

00:01:16.785 --> 00:01:19.871
production workflow. Make every second
grow.

